    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0641" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">196.6/1451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-08-27T17:00:00+03:00">August 27, 1942—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 28—7:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>719. My 330 from Moscow, August 23, 8 p.m. In the absence of Vyshinski who I am
                    informed is ill following an operation for appendicitis which was accompanied by
                    complications, I saw Lozovski<anchor n="49" xml:id="d531-f1"/> yesterday
                    afternoon and discussed with him the gratuities referred to in the Department’s
                    384, August 4, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>I set forth the point of view therein contained and left with Lozovski ah <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> asking that the gratuities be
                    discontinued and at the same time renewing my earlier request that rubles at the
                    diplomatic rate of exchange be made available to the crews of American vessels
                    operating to North Russian ports. Reference is made in this connection to my
                    479, June 3, 11 a.m. Lozovski promised to examine the matter and let me know the
                    decision of the Soviet Government in due course.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d531-f1" n="49" xml:id="d531-f1-content">
                <p>Solomon Abramovich Lozovsky, Assistant People’s Commissar for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
